# Docker build context exclusions. The build context is the repository root
# (see deploy/backend/Dockerfile). deploy/backend/Dockerfile COPYs explicit
# paths rather than `.`, so this is defence in depth — but the first line is
# the one that matters: a real secret must never enter a build context, where
# it survives in image layers and `docker history`.

.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key

node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.github

# build output — the image compiles its own
dist
build
.vite
.docker-build
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# not needed at runtime
docs
.agents
.claude
scripts
*.md
.DS_Store
